codemap 9
tour reader-gui
kind flow
author ai
group gui
note The human's surface as one frame. There is no retained widget tree: every frame the App polls the background work, turns the frame's keys into actions, then builds the element tree for the whole window from the Model - top bar, the panel tree with each panel's front view, status bar, floating picker and tooltip - and hands it to the layout and the renderer. A view never changes the Model: it takes &Model, and a click pushes an Action onto the frame's queue; apply runs the queue once the tree is built, so apply is the one place state changes during a frame. Editing is limited to what a reader needs - deleting a step or a path, pinning a selection from the Source view, creating an empty path - and everything else is typed into the Console as a CLI command. gui-structure lists the rules the modules keep.

step 05p818
order 94
parent jdewtv
author ai
file crates/gui/src/views/document.rs
symbol step_or_reserve
lines 0 55
hash 79d0cb0db0bb8551
note One step in its StepColumn (step_column's id): the header, the note, the code and the gap after them. Built this way the column's height is known next frame, and an Action::Measured stores it in Measures with the step's StepShape. When a measured height for the current shape exists, the step is not selected or being scrolled to, and its column was more than a screen away from the view last frame (near), a reserve of that height stands in instead, so a long document builds only the steps around what is on screen and keeps its scroll extent. A reserved step still reports its link target, so an inlined link under it is drawn.

